- Port from fedora-nexus; portal built for Tumbleweed and Debian Forky/Sid

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 17:16:52 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Ship the noctalia-ui font assets upstream installs
  (/usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal-umbriel/assets/fonts: the tabler icon font,
  its json map and license); the RPM refused to build with them unpackaged.
- Mirror the new Build-Depends into the .dsc: OBS assembles the Debian build
  root from the .dsc list, so libstb-dev and the EGL/GL/pango/xkbcommon
  -dev packages only exist for dpkg-checkbuilddeps when the .dsc carries them.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 17:09:48 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Declare the noctalia-ui dependencies the bundled lib/ actually requires:
  egl/glesv2 (Mesa-libEGL-devel/Mesa-libGLESv2-devel, epoxy is only the
  fallback), wayland-egl, freetype2, fontconfig, cairo-ft, pango >= 1.50,
  pangocairo, pangoft2, harfbuzz, xkbcommon and the stb_image_resize2 header
  (stb-devel). Without them the share picker aborted at
  'lib/meson.build:39: Dependency "epoxy" not found'.
- Debian: the same list as libegl-dev, libgles-dev, libfontconfig-dev,
  libfreetype-dev, libharfbuzz-dev, libpango1.0-dev, libxkbcommon-dev and
  libstb-dev; both suites resolve every pkgconfig module.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 17:00:02 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Fix the build: upstream ed91d04 turned the meson `picker` option from a
  feature into a boolean (meson_options.txt), so `-Dpicker=enabled` now
  aborts with 'Option "picker" value enabled is not boolean'. Pass
  `-Dpicker=true` in the spec and in debian.rules; the option still
  defaults to true, so the share picker stays built.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
